{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:21-9","provision":"BCO 21-9","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"21-9","title":"Section 21-9","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/21-9/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/21-9","current_text":{"html":"<p>In the installation of an ordained minister, the following questions are to be substituted for those addressed to a candidate for ordination, namely: <b>1. Are you now willing to take charge of this congregation as their pastor, agreeable to your declaration in accepting its call?</b> <b>2. Do you conscientiously believe and declare, as far as you know your own heart, that, in taking upon you this charge, you are influenced by a sincere desire to promote the glory of God and the good of the Church?</b> <b>3. Do you solemnly promise that, by the assistance of the grace of God, you will endeavor faithfully to discharge all the duties of a pastor to this congregation, and will be careful to maintain a deportment in all respects becoming a minister of the Gospel of Christ, agreeable to your ordination engagements?</b> <b>Questions to Congregation</b>5 <i>5For assistant minister, address the Session omitting the last phrase of questions 1 and 2.</i></p>","text":"In the installation of an ordained minister, the following questions are to be substituted for those addressed to a candidate for ordination, namely: 1. Are you now willing to take charge of this congregation as their pastor, agreeable to your declaration in accepting its call? 2. Do you conscientiously believe and declare, as far as you know your own heart, that, in taking upon you this charge, you are influenced by a sincere desire to promote the glory of God and the good of the Church? 3. Do you solemnly promise that, by the assistance of the grace of God, you will endeavor faithfully to discharge all the duties of a pastor to this congregation, and will be careful to maintain a deportment in all respects becoming a minister of the Gospel of Christ, agreeable to your ordination engagements? Questions to Congregation5 5For assistant minister, address the Session omitting the last phrase of questions 1 and 2."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"f8bde72b35f9475713a5751081d525f119bc6b4daf3b43ddc86694065015654b","parent_id":"bco:21","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":19,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:21-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Call of assistant pastor from another denomination without presbyterial examination","year":1986,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md:occ-4c3ab877ab72","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"A session may not call an ordained assistant pastor from another denomination without presbytery approval and examination, as all teaching elders must be members of the serving presbytery.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga14_1986__ci16.md"}]},{"id":"bco:21-9--case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Eliot Lee v. Korean Eastern Presbytery","year":2008,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:21-9--case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md:occ-8d574bf2e61a","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.html","repository_path":"cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":155},"excerpt":"This argument fails for numerous reasons. First, the Record of the Case does not indicate a call as pastor, with terms, as required by BCO 20-6, was extended or approved by HKPC and/or submitted to KEP for approval at the 68th Stated Meeting of KEP on October ","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-01_2007-06_2007-07.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["stated supply","interim pastor","pastoral relationship","judicial commission"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-7"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Lee challenged Korean Eastern Presbytery’s actions affecting his interim pastoral relationship, alleging that its October 3, 2006 meeting lacked a quorum. The SJC held the co